The surface charge density is
\[
\sigma=\frac{Q}{A}
=\frac{8.50\times10^{-9}}{0.120}
=7.08\times10^{-8}\,\mathrm{C\,m^{-2}}.
\]
A single large sheet gives field magnitude \(\sigma/(2\epsilon_0)\) on each side. Between the sheets, the fields from the positive and negative sheets point from the positive sheet toward the negative sheet, so they add:
\[
E=\frac{\sigma}{\epsilon_0}
=\frac{7.08\times10^{-8}}{8.85\times10^{-12}}
=8.00\times10^3\,\mathrm{N\,C^{-1}}.
\]
Outside the pair the two sheet fields are equal and opposite, so the approximate external field is zero.
